--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RegenEfficiencyPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable RegenEfficiencyDataSource seam whose methods
keep the web hook names at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles,
useRegenEfficiency ← GET /analytics/regen [start, end], useDrives ← GET /drives?vehicle_id). The web
client-side derivations (getRegenRatio, the date-window `drives` memo, the `monthlyTrend` group-by-
month memo, the `regenDrives` top-20 memo) are ported verbatim into the deterministic, unit-tested
RegenEfficiencyEngine.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
RangePicker date filter) and ALL of the web sections:

  Hero regen-ratio gauge (GlassPanel1 + RadialGauge tinted by the web `regenColor` band + the
  "You've recovered … free charges" info line), the six summary stat tiles (GlassPanel2-7: Total
  Regen / Recovery Rate / Monthly Avg kW / Free Charges / Lifetime Regen kWh / Lifetime Drive kWh —
  the two lifetime tiles always show an em dash exactly as the web hardcodes them null), the
  Monthly-Regen-Trend composed chart (purple drive-count bars + green regen-kWh line, ChartContainer +
  ComposedChart), the regen-metrics bar strip (GlassPanel9: four MetricBars whose value/max fractions
  reproduce the web formulas exactly), and the recent-regen-drives table (GlassPanel10, ratio cells
  tinted by the web `regenColor` band).

All measurements stay SI canonical in the model (meters / watt-hours / watts / m·s⁻¹); conversion to
the user's unit preference happens ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared KMP Units facade
+ RegenEfficiencyFormat (ADR-005). Like the web `useUnits` hook, energy is always shown in kWh and
power in kW (its DEFAULT_ENERGY_PREF / DEFAULT_POWER_PREF), independent of the distance preference.
Adaptive across macOS/iPad regular width vs. iPhone compact (ADR-002/006): the controls, the six-tile
grid, and the four-bar metric strip reflow. Every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings
with the web key names (zero hardcoded text).

Navigation: a dedicated `.regenEfficiency` AppRoute (pathSegment `regen-efficiency`, group `.vehicle`)
so the page is reachable + deep-linkable at /regen-efficiency WITHOUT shadowing the sibling
DriveScorePage, which owns `.driving` (RouteTests still pass — see GATES). Registered via
RegenEfficiencyRouteRegistration in the TeslaSyncApp route-host chain.

There is no map (manifest declares 0 maps). The data sources are request/response, not live SSE
streams, so no staleness indicator applies.

